{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{# S78 step 7 — this page owned its <!DOCTYPE> and <head>. With no layout
   there was nowhere to put a stylesheet link, which is why every one of
   these grew a <style> and every <style> grew literal colours. The shell
   emits the doctype, style.css, the favicon and importmap('app').

   ⚠️ It GAINS Stimulus — the shell emits `importmap('app')` and this page
   did not, so `confirm_controller` and friends now actually run here. A
   delete button wired to a controller that never loaded deletes without
   asking, so that is the fix rather than a side effect. #}

{% block title %}Pages introuvables - Admin FabOS{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/admin.css') ~ '?v=20260817-s144' }}">
    {# S135 — `.miss-pill`, `.miss-path`, `.miss-hits`, `.miss-when`, `.miss-ref`,
       `.miss-tag` and `.miss-empty` are gone: they were this page's private
       spellings of a chip, a monospace value, a number, a date, a quiet line and
       an empty state, all of which the column vocabulary now owns. `.miss-intro`
       and `.miss-actions` stay — an explanatory paragraph and a form row are not
       list furniture.

       ⚠️ This screen's strings are literal French. It sits behind the development
       menu and is not part of the five-language surface; leaving it out of the
       catalogues is the standing rule (UI is translated, this page is a
       diagnostic), not an oversight. #}
    <style>
        .miss-intro { color: var(--color-text-light); margin-bottom: 20px; max-width: 78ch; }
        .miss-actions { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 22px; }
        .miss-path { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; word-break: break-all; }
    </style>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
{% embed 'site/_admin_list.html.twig' with {
    panel_title: 'Adresses demandées',
    panel_note: 'missing_pages.panel_note'|trans({'%count%': misses|length}),
    list_count: misses|length,
    list_route: 'app_admin_missing_pages',
    list_search_placeholder: 'common.search_placeholder'|trans,
    list_client_filter: true,
    list_tiles_label: 'Pourquoi',
    list_tiles: [
        {label: 'admin_list.all'|trans, count: misses|length, category: 'all', active: true},
        {label: 'Fonctionnalité désactivée', count: summary.feature, category: 'feature'},
        {label: 'Lien interne cassé', count: summary.internal, category: 'internal'},
        {label: 'Lien externe', count: summary.external, category: 'external'},
    ],
} %}
    {% block content %}
        {# The whole reason this screen exists: a server log shows these two as
           the same event, and they call for opposite responses. #}
        <p class="miss-intro">
            Deux choses très différentes produisent la même erreur 404. Un <strong>lien cassé</strong> dans vos
            propres pages est une correction à faire. Quelqu'un qui <strong>cherche une fonctionnalité que vous
            avez désactivée</strong> n'est pas un bug — c'est exactement ce que fait le gating — mais c'est une
            demande, et la réponse est sur l'écran <a href="{{ path('app_admin_features') }}">Fonctionnalités</a>,
            pas dans les gabarits.
        </p>

        {% set labels = {'feature': 'Fonctionnalité désactivée', 'internal': 'Lien interne cassé', 'external': 'Lien externe'} %}
        {% set signals = {'feature': 'wait', 'internal': 'stop', 'external': 'muted'} %}
        {% embed 'site/_data_table.html.twig' with {
            columns: [
                {label: 'Adresse demandée', class: 'is-grow'},
                {label: 'Pourquoi', class: 'is-tight'},
                {label: 'Demandes', numeric: true, class: 'is-tight'},
                {label: 'Vue', class: 'is-tight'},
            ],
            rows: misses,
            empty: 'Rien pour l’instant. Seules sont enregistrées les adresses qui n’ont correspondu à aucune route, et seulement quand elles arrivent avec une page d’origine ou visent une fonctionnalité désactivée : les sondages de robots n’apparaissent pas ici.',
        } %}
            {% block rows %}
                {% for miss in misses %}
                    <tr data-admin-list-filter-row data-admin-list-filter-category="{{ miss.reason }}">
                        <td>{% include 'site/_cell_title.html.twig' with {
                            title: miss.path,
                            subtitle: miss.lastReferrer|default(''),
                        } only %}</td>
                        <td>{% include 'site/_cell_state.html.twig' with {
                            label: labels[miss.reason]|default(miss.reason),
                            signal: signals[miss.reason]|default('muted'),
                        } only %}</td>
                        <td class="is-numeric">{{ miss.hits }}</td>
                        <td>{% include 'site/_cell_date.html.twig' with {
                            value: miss.lastSeen, convention: 'machine',
                            subtitle: miss.firstSeen ? 'depuis le ' ~ miss.firstSeen|lab_date('d/m/Y') : '',
                        } only %}</td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            {% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}
    {% endblock %}
    {% block panel_extra %}
        {# Aggregation keeps the table small on its own — one row per distinct URL,
           whatever the traffic — so these are about relevance, not size. #}
        <form method="post" class="miss-actions">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('admin_missing_pages') }}">
            <button type="submit" name="action" value="prune" class="btn-link">Oublier ce qui dort depuis 90 jours</button>
            <button type="submit" name="action" value="clear" class="btn-link btn-danger-admin"
                    data-controller="confirm" data-confirm-message-value="Vider tout le journal des pages introuvables ?" data-action="click->confirm#ask">Vider le journal</button>
        </form>
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
{% endblock %}
